{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vectors for the stretched Dialog actions row (CoreDialogActionsLayout.stretch).",
    "Read by coui_core (CoreDialogActionsStretch.place), coui_flutter (the Dialog",
    "actions render object) and a real-Chrome probe of the Web footer CSS, so a fix",
    "that lands on one platform fails the other.",
    "Each action is a row of parts, laid side by side and wrapping between them:",
    "its narrowest width (min-content) is its widest part, its natural width",
    "(max-content) is the sum of its parts. Every part is partHeight tall, or the",
    "action's own partHeight when it states one.",
    "cells: line (row from 0), start (offset of the action's start edge from the",
    "row's start edge: left in ltr, right in rtl) and width, in logical px.",
    "flutterCells, where present, is what Flutter draws instead: Flutter never lays",
    "an action out wider than its row, so an action that cannot be narrower than",
    "the row is squeezed to it there, while CSS lets it overflow at the start."
  ],
  "spacing": 8,
  "runSpacing": 8,
  "partHeight": 40,
